he subtraction over the matrices in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(B+A)-(B-C)-A & =B+A-B+C-A \\\\  & =\\cancel{B}+\\cancel{A}-\\cancel{B}+C-\\cancel{A} \\\\  & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are left with a single matrix. So, the result is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ 8 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Sum or Difference of Three or More Matrices Using Distributivity"} :step/id #uuid "fe37dd78-b6d7-5cd1-8c23-51e67c1d3bbe" :step/math-academy-id 464517}] :activity/title "Properties of Matrix Addition" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186101035}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186048863 :topic/difficulty 0.6044133585735892 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428134 :encompassing/rationale "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 1 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1 (1/1). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: False. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/foundations-frequency-estimates.json, pair 1168->29. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." :encompassing/topic {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049304} :encompassing/weight 1.0}] :topic/id #uuid "c769a4f9-fb8c-5389-aac8-802ee9b0afb4" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100991 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100686 :question/id #uuid "0928c2fa-a772-5d39-a638-1b1d0e71be2f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4378" :question/problem "Calculate $A-(B-C),$ where\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Performing the operations on each corresponding entry, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(B-C) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}-(\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-1-0 & -1-(-5) \\\\ 2-1 & 0-1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1-(-1) & 0-4 \\\\ 2-1 & -2-(-1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "667ac53c-36b8-56a0-9699-fe27c8373c6b" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049304}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549194 :question-generator/id #uuid "dc71b24c-40dc-53be-9574-40a00b2b2f9c" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186100991.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101106 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "850af764-4ddb-53d3-a63a-0f8b3db18d54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097972} {:answer/id #uuid "8e99ffbb-c95b-55f0-9ddd-98f9bebe3612" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097973} {:answer/id #uuid "d0f41abb-2f98-5827-a0ee-deaf9afa93b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186